  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Hey Team! \n\nIs there a way we can make it more clear to the end user that they have been banned from a group instance rather then the actual world as a whole? \n\nOn a daily I get (usually rude) messages from users that they have been \"banned\" from my worlds. To which I have to explain that we can not ban users from worlds and that they have been likely banned via the group system that is hosting an instance in the world. \n\nIs there any way this can be made more clear to the end user? \n\nMaybe a pop up message along the lines of: \n\n\"You have been banned by (group name) and will not be able to join any instance hosted by this group. Please try and load a different instance of (world name) to join!\" or something along those lines?\n\nThanks so much! ^^",
